The $\%$ symbol means percent, which is per hundred.

$\begin{align}
25\text{ per }100&=\dfrac{25}{100}\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{4} \cdot \dfrac{25}{25}\\\\
&=\dfrac{1}{4}
\end{align}$

The $\%$ symbol means percent, which is per hundred.

$\begin{align}
75\text{ per }100&=\dfrac{75}{100}\\\\
&=\dfrac{3}{4} \cdot \dfrac{25}{25}\\\\
&=\dfrac{3}{4}
\end{align}$
